  "content": "Here is the step-by-step deterministic arithmetic solution for the given values:\n\n**Given:**\n*   $a = 137$\n*   $b = 29$\n*   $c = 11$\n\n**Expression to compute:**\n$$(a \\cdot b + c^3) - (a - b) \\cdot c$$\n\n### Step 1: Compute $a \\cdot b$\n$$137 \\cdot 29$$\n\nBreaking it down:\n$$137 \\cdot 29 = 137 \\cdot (30 - 1) = (137 \\cdot 30) - 137$$\n$$137 \\cdot 30 = 4110$$\n$$4110 - 137 = 3973$$\n\nSo, **$a \\cdot b = 3973$**.\n\n### Step 2: Compute $c^3$\n$$11^3 = 11 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 11$$\n$$11 \\cdot 11 = 121$$\n$$121 \\cdot 11 = 1331$$\n\nSo, **$c^3 = 1331$**.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the first parenthesis $(a \\cdot b + c^3)$\n$$3973 + 1331$$\n\nLet's add them:\n  $$3973$$\n$$+1331$$\n-------\n$$5304$$\n\nSo, **$(a \\cdot b + c^3) = 5304$**.\n\n### Step 4: Compute $(a - b)$\n$$137 - 29$$\n\n$$137 - 29 = 108$$\n\nSo, **$(a - b) = 108$**.\n\n### Step 5: Compute the second part $(a - b) \\cdot c$\n$$108 \\cdot 11$$\n\n$$108 \\cdot 11 = 108 \\cdot (10 + 1) = 1080 + 108 = 1188$$\n\nSo, **$(a - b) \\cdot c = 1188$**.\n\n",
